  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Demon hunters has the ability to cast a small number of divine spells which are drawn from the demon hunter spell list presented at the end of this document. A demon hunter must choose and prepare her spells in advance.</p>\n<p>To ready or cast a spell, a demon hunter must have a Charisma score of at least 10 + the spell’s level. The Difficulty Class for a saving throw against a demon hunter’s spell is 10 + the spell’s level + the demon hunter’s Charisma modifier. Bonus spells for demon hunters rely on her Charisma score.</p>\n<p><strong>Material Component:</strong> A demon hunter must use strips of paper, called ofuda, with her spells written on them as material components to focus the power of her magic (see <a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/sutra-magic\">Sutra Magic</a>). Casting spells without a prepared material component (an ofuda) increases the casting time for all of the demon hunter’s spells. (Spells with a casting time of one standard action or less would take a full round to cast.)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/demon-hunter#toc2\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
